From: Lewis Gibson <12851394+lewisgibson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:20:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Make CommandStorage namespaces a ConcurrentHashMap

CommandStorage lazily loads a namespace's container into a plain HashMap
the first time it is read. Loot tables with a storage nbt or number
provider and text components with a storage source read it from whichever
region is running them, so two regions reading a namespace for the first
time at once race on the put. Make the map concurrent, like the saved
data storage cache it loads from.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/storage/CommandStorage.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/storage/CommandStorage.java
index c99b9001cefdf6992dfcbe90294f697fe3b2eb64..7c868c0a49c1ecaed66a3faed7c7044829b9d66e 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/storage/CommandStorage.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/storage/CommandStorage.java
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ import org.jspecify.annotations.Nullable;
 
 public class CommandStorage {
     private static final String COMMAND_STORAGE = "command_storage";
-    private final Map<String, CommandStorage.Container> namespaces = new HashMap<>();
+    private final Map<String, CommandStorage.Container> namespaces = new java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap<>(); // Folia - region threading - read from every region by loot nbt providers and text components
     private final SavedDataStorage savedDataStorage;
 
     public CommandStorage(final SavedDataStorage savedDataStorage) {
